  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Find the number of arrangements of BOOKKEEPER if",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "there are no restrictions.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$151\\,200$",
          "worked": "There are 10 letters, with two O’s, two K’s and three E’s.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{10!}{2!\\times2!\\times3!}\\\\N&=151\\,200.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "all the vowels are together.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3600$\n\nArrange the vowel block with the consonants, then multiply by its internal arrangements.",
          "worked": "The vowel block contains three E’s and two O’s. Arrange the block with B, K, K, P and R, dividing by $2!$ for the K’s. The block has $5!/(3!\\times2!)$ internal arrangements.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{6!}{2!}\\times\\frac{5!}{3!\\times2!}\\\\N&=360\\times10\\\\N&=3600.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the O’s are together and the K’s are together.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6720$\n\nTreat OO and KK as two distinct blocks.",
          "worked": "Treat OO and KK as single elements. Together with B, E, E, E, P and R, there are eight elements, including three identical E’s.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{8!}{3!}\\\\N&=6720.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q14-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "the vowels appear in alphabetical order (all E’s before all O’s), not necessarily together.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$15\\,120$\n\nOnly one of the $5!/(3!\\times2!)=10$ possible vowel orders has all E’s before all O’s.",
          "worked": "For each choice of vowel positions, the vowels have $5!/(3!\\times2!)=10$ distinct orders. Only EEEOO is allowed.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{10!}{2!\\times2!\\times3!}\\div\\frac{5!}{3!\\times2!}\\\\N&=151\\,200\\div10\\\\N&=15\\,120.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
